# MemoryWeave — Cursor Rules
# AI-powered Organizational Memory & Operational Intelligence Platform
# Hackathon Edition | React + Vite + FastAPI + Neo4j + ChromaDB + Claude API

## Project Identity

MemoryWeave is an enterprise SaaS platform that preserves organizational memory
using AI agents, knowledge graphs, and semantic retrieval. It prevents knowledge
loss when employees leave by extracting workflows, dependencies, and institutional
knowledge from Slack, GitHub, incidents, and internal docs.

The design source of truth is `_design-reference.html` in the repo root.
Every UI decision must be traceable to that file. When in doubt, check it.

---

## Critical Rules (Never Break These)

1. Use a hybrid approach: Tailwind for layout, spacing, and flex/grid utilities.
 Use CSS variable inline styles for all design token values — colors, shadows, border-radius, typography. 
 Never replace a CSS variable with a Tailwind color, shadow, or radius class. 
 The design system lives in CSS variables, not Tailwind's config.

2. NEVER deviate from the design token system. Every color, shadow, radius, and
   font must use CSS variables defined in `src/index.css`. No hardcoded hex values
   in components except for sidebar-specific colors (#111110, rgba(255,255,255,x)).

3. NEVER use Inter, Roboto, Arial, or system fonts as primary typefaces.
   DM Sans is the sans font. DM Mono is the mono font. Always.

4. NEVER create new animation keyframes. All animations are defined globally in
   `src/index.css`. Reference them by name: fadeUp, fadeIn, slideRight, pulse-dot,
   float, shimmer, dashFlow, nodeAppear, graphPulse.

5. NEVER import or install a CSS framework, UI kit (MUI, Chakra, shadcn, Ant),
   or chart library other than Recharts. The graph is custom SVG — not
   react-force-graph, not D3, not vis-network.

6. NEVER use localStorage or sessionStorage. All state lives in Zustand.

7. NEVER write API calls directly in components. All API calls go through
   service functions in `src/services/api.js`.

