## Code Commenting Rules

Every file must be commented. These are the minimum requirements:

### File Header Comment (every .jsx and .py file)
```javascript
/**
 * ComponentName.jsx
 * 
 * [One-line description of what this file does]
 * 
 * Used by: [which pages or components use this]
 * Depends on: [key dependencies — store slices, services, other components]
 */
```

### Function/Component Comments
- Every React component: one-line JSDoc above it explaining its purpose and key props
- Every custom hook: explain what it manages and what it returns
- Every utility function: explain inputs, outputs, and any gotchas

### Inline Comments
- Comment any non-obvious logic (graph traversal, animation math, regex)
- Comment all TODO items with format: `// TODO [Phase X]: description`
- Comment all Codex territory stubs: `// CODEX: this function is implemented in agents/`
- Comment all mock data placeholders: `// MOCK: replace with api.fetchX() in Phase 4`

### Example (required style)
```javascript
/**
 * FullKnowledgeGraph.jsx
 * 
 * Interactive SVG knowledge graph with filter, click-to-select, and detail panel.
 * Renders nodes by type (person/system/incident/workflow) with glow effects.
 * 
 * Used by: GraphPage
 * Depends on: appStore (graphNodes, graphEdges, selectedNode, filterType)
 */

/**
 * Computes edge visibility based on the active filter type.
 * An edge is visible only if BOTH connected nodes pass the current filter.
 * This prevents orphaned visible edges when nodes are filtered out.
 */
function isEdgeVisible(edge, nodes, filterType) {
  if (filterType === 'all') return true
  const fromNode = nodes.find(n => n.id === edge.from)
  const toNode = nodes.find(n => n.id === edge.to)
  return fromNode?.type === filterType || toNode?.type === filterType
}
```

